      "description": "Watch Stoke City vs Swansea City highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The atmosphere at the Bet365 Stadium was expectant as Stoke City hosted Swansea City in a high-stakes Championship encounter. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish their authority early in the season, setting the stage for a tactical battle defined by clinical finishing and bench depth. Early Exchanges and Instant Responses The match kicked off on August 15, 2026 , with the home side finding their rhythm almost immediately. In the 10th minute, Stoke City broke the deadlock when Tomas Rigo provided a clever assist for Eric Bocat , who made no mistake in slotting the ball home. The lead, however, was short-lived as Swansea City began to find gaps in the Potters' defense. Their persistence paid off in the 23rd minute; Zan Vipotnik turned provider for Joseph Opoku , who finished calmly to level the scores and silence the home crowd. As the first half progressed, the intensity grew, leading to a yellow card for Stoke's Luke Graham in the 36th minute. Despite several close chances for both teams, the sides remained deadlocked at 1-1 heading into the interval after a lengthy period of stoppage time. Substitute Heroics Turn the Tide The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to break the impasse. Swansea City made a decisive triple substitution in the 65th minute, introducing Adam Idah to lead the line. The move proved to be a masterstroke. Just a minute later, Josh Tymon delivered a pinpoint cross that Adam Idah expertly converted to put the visitors ahead for the first time in the match. Stoke City attempted to claw their way back, introducing Jun-Ho Bae and Robert Bozenik to bolster their attack, but the Swans' backline held firm. The closing stages were frantic, characterized by defensive resilience and a flurry of bookings for Swansea's Melker Widell and Josh Tymon . After six minutes of added time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a hard-earned victory for the visiting side."
